 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Dialogue: At the school gate, March 2020\nBIH: Why is everybody wearing a mask today?\nNURSE NJI: Because of COVID-19. It is a new disease caused by a virus. It started in one country and spread all over the world, so it is a pandemic.\nBIH: How does it spread?\nNURSE NJI: Through tiny drops when a sick person coughs, sneezes or talks. That is why we wash our hands with soap, cover our mouths when we cough and keep a distance of one metre.\nBIH: Can it be cured?\nNURSE NJI: Most people get better, but old people and the sick can die. Now there are vaccines. Stay calm, follow the rules and protect others.\n\nAn epidemic spreads quickly in one area; a pandemic spreads across the world; an endemic disease (malaria in Cameroon) is always present in a region.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "In the dialogue, why does the nurse call COVID-{19} a pandemic?",
  "steps": [
   "A pandemic spreads across many countries or the whole world.",
   "The nurse says it started in one country and spread all over the world."
  ],
  "answer": "Because it spread all over the world.",
  "checks": []
 },
